764
00:39:43,460 --> 00:39:46,500
我只有一线渺茫的胜算。
I have just one slim chance.

765
00:39:46,540 --> 00:39:50,180
他们走的路程得比我远。
They've got to go further than me.

766
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:54,220
他们坐的火车现在开始绕来绕去，
尽往火车自己想去的地方跑，
They're on a train which is gonna wiggle
around now, going where IT wants to go,

767
00:39:54,260 --> 00:39:56,180
而不是他们想去的地方。
not where THEY want to go.

768
00:39:56,220 --> 00:39:59,980
至于我呢，
则是直奔目标，
Me, on the other hand,
I'm proceeding directly,

769
00:40:00,020 --> 00:40:04,100
路上再不用加油，直插蒙特卡洛。
no more fuel stops, to Monte-Carlo.

770
00:40:04,140 --> 00:40:06,740
所以先别急着把赌注全押在火车上。
So don't bet on the train just yet.

771
00:40:08,460 --> 00:40:11,340
好了，现在我已经杀到了法国南部，
Okay, now that I'm down in the south,

772
00:40:11,380 --> 00:40:15,100
正开在通往蒙特卡洛的弯曲高速上，
on the twisty motorway going up
to Monte-Carlo,

773
00:40:15,140 --> 00:40:18,300
这辆车已经从一台舒适的长途巡航座驾，
the car's changed from being a comfortable
long-distance cruiser

774
00:40:18,340 --> 00:40:22,300
彻底蜕变成了一头野性十足的狂暴跑车。
into being this kind of savage sports car.

775
00:40:22,340 --> 00:40:26,260
它开起来就像一头猛兽，
而这正是一台阿斯顿该有的滋味。
It feels like a brute, which is exactly
what an Aston should feel like.

776
00:40:28,220 --> 00:40:32,300
哈蒙德：距离终点还剩100英里，
火车沿着海岸线慢了下来，
HAMMOND: With 100 miles to go, the train
slows down along the coast,

777
00:40:32,340 --> 00:40:35,820
两边的差距开始被缩短了。
and the gap is starting to shrink.

778
00:40:35,860 --> 00:40:39,900
到了尼斯，尽管离蒙特卡洛只有15英里，
And at Nice, even though we're just
15 miles from Monte-Carlo,

779
00:40:39,940 --> 00:40:42,380
我们还得再倒一次火车。
we need to make another train change.

780
00:40:43,740 --> 00:40:46,180
别再晃来晃去了。
- 我停不下来。
Stop pacing now.
- I can't.

781
00:40:46,220 --> 00:40:50,020
我对这辆车已经不只是喜欢了，简直是爱死它了。
I don't just like this car, I love it.

782
00:40:50,060 --> 00:40:53,300
此时此刻，杰里米肯定正一边开一边……
[低吼]
梅：我知道。
Right now, Jeremy's going...
[GROWLS]
MAY: I know.

783
00:40:55,300 --> 00:40:56,820
[用力哼气]
[GRUNTING]

784
00:40:56,860 --> 00:40:58,140
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE ROARS]

785
00:40:58,180 --> 00:41:01,820
这感觉简直是机械驾驶的终极形态。
It feels like motoring perfection.

786
00:41:01,860 --> 00:41:04,900
法国佬，麻烦借过挪个道成吗？
If you don't mind just getting
out of the way, Frenchie.

787
00:41:04,940 --> 00:41:06,780
我还赶着去堵火车呢。
I've got a train to catch.

788
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:09,800
♪ Craig Armstrong - Ruthless Gravity ♪
♪ Craig Armstrong - Ruthless Gravity ♪

789
00:41:19,780 --> 00:41:21,300
[引擎狂飙轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVVING]

790
00:41:24,060 --> 00:41:25,300
继续往上冲！
Keep going up!

791
00:41:27,580 --> 00:41:28,820
哈蒙德：快跑！
- 到了到了，就是这里！
HAMMOND: Go!
- This is it. This is it.

792
00:41:30,260 --> 00:41:33,100
哈蒙德：快点啊，詹姆斯！
要是这时候给输了……
HAMMOND: Come on, James.
To lose it now...

793
00:41:33,140 --> 00:41:34,780
这该死的破包！
This sodding bag!

794
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:39,340
快点！最后一段了，就在下边！
Come on! Last bit. It is down here.

795
00:41:40,780 --> 00:41:42,260
哈蒙德：搞快点！
HAMMOND: Come on!

796
00:41:44,300 --> 00:41:45,380
噢！哎哟！
Ooh! Ooh!

797
00:41:47,220 --> 00:41:48,900
我们当初怎么就没带份地图呢？
Why didn't we bring a map?

798
00:41:49,820 --> 00:41:51,340
詹姆斯！快跟上！
James! Come on!

799
00:41:53,340 --> 00:41:54,780
噢，这下完蛋了。
Oh, that's bad.

800
00:41:57,300 --> 00:41:59,860
唉，我真不忍心告诉他这个噩耗。
Oh, I haven't the heart to tell him.

801
00:42:02,140 --> 00:42:04,660
一切都结束了，伙计。
- 哎呀，见鬼。
It's all over, mate.
- Oh, cock.

802
00:42:04,680 --> 00:42:06,560
[哈蒙德吃吃傻笑]
[HAMMOND CHORTLES]

803
00:42:06,580 --> 00:42:07,940
晚上好啊。
Evening.

804
00:42:07,980 --> 00:42:10,100
克拉克森：不知道你们注意到没有。
CLARKSON: I don't know if you've
noticed something here.

805
00:42:10,140 --> 00:42:13,100
你们俩看起来又累又抓狂，
而我却惬意得很。
You two look very stressed and tired,
I'm very relaxed.

806
00:42:13,140 --> 00:42:14,500
确实出了不少汗啊。
There is a degree of perspiration going on.

807
00:42:14,540 --> 00:42:16,660
我觉得今天我们证明的最重要的一点，
I think the important thing
that we've proved today

808
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:19,740
就是无论公共交通有多棒，
is that no matter how good
public transport is,

809
00:42:19,780 --> 00:42:22,180
无论它运行得有多么分秒不差，
no matter how much it runs like clockwork,

810
00:42:22,220 --> 00:42:24,620
也永远比不过一辆车。
it'll never be a match for a car.

811
00:42:27,300 --> 00:42:29,940
而且我们用来证明这一点的，是何等尤物啊，
And what a car we used to prove the point,

812
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:32,380
那辆糊满死苍蝇的DB9，
the fly-spattered DB9,

813
00:42:32,420 --> 00:42:37,260
它可不仅仅是比火车强……
which isn't just better than a train...

814
00:42:37,300 --> 00:42:41,420
它比宾利欧陆GT更讨人喜欢、更全面。
It's more loveable and it's more rounded
than a Bentley Continental GT.

815
00:42:41,460 --> 00:42:44,060
它比法拉利575更棒。
It's better than a Ferrari 575.

816
00:42:44,100 --> 00:42:46,400
它比Vanquish更好，
主要是因为它拥有
It's better than a Vanquish,
principally because it's got

817
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:48,340
更好的变速箱，而且长得更俊，
a better gearbox and it's prettier,

818
00:42:48,380 --> 00:42:50,780
并且只要103,000英镑，
and at £103,000,

819
00:42:50,820 --> 00:42:54,460
比起所有对手都要便宜得多。
it's considerably less expensive
than all its rivals.

820
00:42:54,500 --> 00:42:56,860
但你知道它最绝的地方是什么吗？
But you know the best thing about it?

821
00:42:56,900 --> 00:43:00,660
它是一台如假包换、百分百正宗、货真价实的，
It's a proper, pukka, 100%, real,

822
00:43:00,700 --> 00:43:05,900
妙不可言、璀璨夺目、精美绝伦、气势恢宏的阿斯顿·马丁。
fabulous, glorious, exquisite,
magnificent Aston Martin.

823
00:43:11,340 --> 00:43:13,420
所以这下总算弄明白了，对吧？
So we have managed to clear that up. Okay?

824
00:43:13,460 --> 00:43:15,700
阿斯顿·马丁就是比火车强。
An Aston is better than a train.

825
00:43:15,740 --> 00:43:17,660
现在该来梳理一下
阿斯顿·马丁的产品阵容了。
Now it's time to clear up
the Aston Martin range.

826
00:43:17,700 --> 00:43:21,500
以前这事儿特简单，因为他们
只造一款车。
It used to be very simple because they
only made one car.

827
00:43:21,540 --> 00:43:23,500
不，说真的，他们过去真的只造这一款车。
No, really, they only did make one car.

828
00:43:23,540 --> 00:43:26,740
但现在他们抱上了福特的金主大腿，
瞧瞧这个，造了三款！
But now they've got Ford money,
look at this, they make three!

829
00:43:26,780 --> 00:43:29,700
而且它们长得全都一模一样！
And they all look exactly the same!

830
00:43:29,740 --> 00:43:31,260
呃，但还是有微妙区别的。
Er, but there are subtle differences.

831
00:43:31,300 --> 00:43:34,300
这是Vanquish，售价160,000英镑，
This is the Vanquish. £160,000,

832
00:43:34,340 --> 00:43:38,500
V12发动机，贼（V）蠢的变速箱，
贼（V）受足球明星欢迎。
V12 engine, V silly gearbox,
V popular with footballers.

833
00:43:38,540 --> 00:43:42,820
这是DB9。
快得飞起，
发动机跟那台一模一样，
This is the DB9.
Very, very fast,
same engine as that,

834
00:43:42,860 --> 00:43:44,820
硬顶版卖103,000英镑，
£103,000 for the hardtop,

835
00:43:44,860 --> 00:43:47,460
敞篷版则是
107,000英镑。
and £107,000 for
the convertible version.

836
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:50,100
到了明年，
我们就能迎来这个了！
And then next year,
we're getting this!

837
00:43:50,140 --> 00:43:52,300
阿斯顿·马丁V8 Vantage。
The AM V8 Vantage.

838
00:43:52,340 --> 00:43:54,980
那台只要70,000英镑！
That's gonna be £70,000!

839
00:43:55,020 --> 00:43:56,420
直接硬刚911！
Going against the 911!

840
00:43:56,460 --> 00:43:58,780
而且它还会有
敞篷版本！
And there'll be
a convertible version!

841
00:43:58,820 --> 00:44:04,260
所以说到底，我的意思就是：
全世界最好的三辆车，全都是英国造的！
So really what I'm saying is, the three
best cars in the world are all British!

842
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:06,820
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

843
00:44:06,840 --> 00:44:08,840
[掌声]
[APPLAUSE]

844
00:44:11,460 --> 00:44:16,340
好了。重大时刻，新一季开播，
酷车墙强势回归！我很欣慰。
Right. Big moment, new series and it's the
return of the Cool Wall! I'm very pleased.

845
00:44:16,420 --> 00:44:17,660
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

846
00:44:19,180 --> 00:44:22,380
哈蒙德：呃，能看到它回归
真是太棒了。
HAMMOND: It's uh, it's brilliant
to see it back.

847
00:44:22,420 --> 00:44:23,940
咱们弄点新货上墙吧。
Let's get some new stuff on the wall.

848
00:44:23,980 --> 00:44:27,780
首先，大家前面已经在节目里见识过了：
城市罗孚（CityRover）。
And, first of all, we saw it earlier on:
the CityRover.

849
00:44:27,820 --> 00:44:30,020
[观众起哄发嘘声]
克拉克森：极度不酷？
[AUDIENCE JEERING]
CLARKSON: Seriously Uncool?

850
00:44:30,060 --> 00:44:32,860
哈蒙德：简直就是垃圾，没错。
关键在于，它甚至都不是一辆正经罗孚，
HAMMOND: It's rubbish, yes.
I mean the problem is, it's not
even a real Rover,

851
00:44:32,900 --> 00:44:37,220
所以它纯粹是在硬装成某种
反正本来就很不酷的东西。
so it's actually TRYING to be something
that's uncool anyway.

852
00:44:37,260 --> 00:44:38,860
坦白讲，这绝对没跑了。对吧？
Which, frankly, it's gotta be. Is it?

853
00:44:38,900 --> 00:44:41,820
它是不酷呢，还是……
观众：极度不酷！
Is it Uncool, or is it...
AUDIENCE: Seriously Uncool.

854
00:44:41,860 --> 00:44:44,980
平常我倒挺喜欢跟现场观众
抬抬杠，到处走走拌两句嘴……
Normally, I like to argue
with the audience,
go around, have a bit...

855
00:44:45,020 --> 00:44:46,340
但这次不用争了，你们说得对。
But, no, you're right.

856
00:44:46,380 --> 00:44:48,220
那确实是极度不酷。
- 确实。
That is Seriously Uncool.
- It is.

857
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:51,040
克拉克森：下一辆是什么？
- 我这儿有一辆，福特嘉年华ST。
CLARKSON: What's next?
- I've got one, the Ford Fiesta ST.

858
00:44:51,060 --> 00:44:52,860
前面节目里我们也见过了。
[观众起哄叹气]
We saw that earlier on in the programme.
[AUDIENCE GROANS]

859
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:55,580
好啦，你们瞧……
- 大家觉得如何？
Well, now, you see...
- What do we think?

860
00:44:55,600 --> 00:44:58,100
这次我往这边走走……
大家觉得这车怎么样？
I'll come over here this time...
what do we think on that?

861
00:44:58,120 --> 00:45:00,520
男观众：不酷。因为是福特。
- 不……凭什么啊？
MAN: Uncool. It's a Ford.
- Unco- why?

862
00:45:00,540 --> 00:45:03,040
怎么就？
[观众笑声]
What?
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

863
00:45:03,060 --> 00:45:05,060
[孤零零的掌声]
[SINGULAR CLAPPING]

864
00:45:06,500 --> 00:45:09,000
我们在这节目里早就定论了，好吗，
福特车挺好的。
We've established on this show, right,
Fords are fine.

865
00:45:09,020 --> 00:45:12,620
动动你的榆木脑袋记牢点。
你，你觉得呢？
Try to get that into your thick skull.
You, what do you think?

866
00:45:12,640 --> 00:45:14,640
我觉得它介于“酷”和“不酷”之间。
I think it's in-between Cool and Uncool.

867
00:45:14,660 --> 00:45:16,660
顺便，既然我走过来了，城市罗孚呢？
你觉得那车怎么样？
Actually, while I'm here, CityRover;
what do you think of that?

868
00:45:16,680 --> 00:45:19,180
男观众：呃……
- 你是印度人吧？
MAN: Umm...
- Are you actually an Indian?

869
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:21,200
是的。
- 干得漂亮，哥们。[笑]
Yeah.
- Well done, mate. [LAUGHING]

870
00:45:21,220 --> 00:45:23,720
克拉克森：你懂我意思吧？
简直笑死人！
CLARKSON: You know what I mean?
What a laugh!

871
00:45:23,744 --> 00:45:27,244
哈蒙德：行吧，好吧……
- 也许再过几周它就变酷了，
HAMMOND: Yeah, okay...
- It could be cool in a few weeks' time,

872
00:45:27,260 --> 00:45:29,260
而且，要知道——
- 在孟买它兴许算酷！
and, you know-
- It could be cool in Bombay!

873
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:32,780
不，过几周在这儿也可能变酷，
到时候指不定算复古风还是什么的。
No, it could be cool here in a few weeks'
time when it's probably retro or something.

874
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:35,200
哈蒙德：复古？！
- 或者随便什么吧。
HAMMOND: Retro!?
- Or something.

875
00:45:35,220 --> 00:45:37,620
因为你以前住——你在印度生活过吗？
- 呃，生活过。
'Cause were you living- have you ever lived
in India?
- Yeah I have.

876
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:42,240
好，那你还记得当年罗孚把蒙特哥卖给你们吗？
这根本就是报复，对吧？
Ok, do you remember when Rover sold you
the Montego? That is payback, isn't it?

877
00:45:42,260 --> 00:45:44,560
[观众大笑]
还是柴油版蒙特哥！
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
The Montego Diesel!

878
00:45:44,580 --> 00:45:47,080
不管怎么说，你觉得福特怎么样？那个——
- 酷。
What do you think of the Ford, anyway? The-
- Cool.

879
00:45:47,100 --> 00:45:48,400
你觉得它酷？
- 除了名字以外。
You think it's cool?
- Apart from the name.

880
00:45:48,420 --> 00:45:50,920
除了名字？ST这名字？
- 嗯，对啊！
Apart from the name? The ST?
- Mmmm. Yeah!

881
00:45:50,940 --> 00:45:52,140
嗯，确实。
- 这是个问题。
Hmm. Quite.
- It is a problem.

882
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:55,460
这车挺让人纠结的，因为它是一辆欧洲掀背小车，
按理说应该……
It's a difficult one because it's a small
European hatchback which should mean that

883
00:45:55,480 --> 00:45:59,880
往……这边放，但它根本配不上。
- 没错，而且问题还不单单出在名字上，对吧？
it goes... this way, but it just doesn't.
- No, it's not just the name, is it?

884
00:45:59,900 --> 00:46:01,800
哈蒙德：这可是XR2，对吧？
- 对，它是辆XR2，而且不光是这个，
HAMMOND: It's the XR2, isn't it?
- Yeah, it's an XR2 and it's not just,

885
00:46:01,820 --> 00:46:04,320
你看关键在于，福特刚才通知我了，
我能提到那台GT了，
you see the thing is, they've now told me,
Ford, that I'm getting the GT

886
00:46:04,340 --> 00:46:06,340
所以我现在想怎么损就怎么损……
[观众笑声]
so I can say what I like...
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

887
00:46:07,064 --> 00:46:09,064
哈蒙德：你把它扔到“不酷”区了，行吧。
- 它就是“不酷”。
HAMMOND: You have it at Uncool, yeah.
- That's Uncool.

888
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:11,880
克拉克森：下一个是什么？哦。
- 好，这个可太简单了：
CLARKSON: What have we got next? Ooh.
- Right, this is a very easy one:

889
00:46:11,960 --> 00:46:13,200
法拉利。
- 这不就来了嘛，闭着眼都能选。
Ferrari.
- There we go. Very easy.

890
00:46:13,240 --> 00:46:15,440
这是一台法拉利 612 Scaglietti。
[观众：酷！极酷！]
This is a Ferrari 612 Scaglietti.
[AUDIENCE MEMBER: COOL! SUB-ZERO!]

891
00:46:15,480 --> 00:46:19,200
听着，这是一台工艺精湛、
优雅高贵的四座法拉利，
Now, this is a sophisticated,
elegant, four-seater Ferrari,

892
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:21,360
作为456的继任者，简直美极了。
replaces the 456, absolutely beautiful.

893
00:46:21,400 --> 00:46:25,120
这显然很“酷”，甚至够得上“极酷”。
This clearly is Cool, if not Sub Zero.

894
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:26,960
正如我们在上一季说过的，
As we said in the last series,

895
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:29,000
它的设计师——我真没开玩笑——
this was styled, and I'm not joking,

896
00:46:29,040 --> 00:46:31,080
居然叫肯。
by a man called Ken.

897
00:46:31,120 --> 00:46:32,600
这可就成问题了。
That is a problem.

898
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:35,120
说真的，“肯”是个好名字，
如果你是个足球裁判的话。
Now, Ken is a good name
if you're a football referee.

899
00:46:35,160 --> 00:46:37,440
如果你是个粉刷匠，这名字也不错。
- 扯淡！等等！
It's a good name if you're a plasterer.
- No! Hang on!

900
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:39,920
但法拉利设计师？这名字一点都不酷！
- 不对！
But a Ferrari designer? It's not cool!
- No!

901
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:42,080
胡说，历史上明明有很酷的“肯”，见鬼。
No, there's been some cool Kens, damn it.

902
00:46:42,120 --> 00:46:43,200
那你随口说一个叫肯的酷人。
Name a cool Ken.

903
00:46:43,240 --> 00:46:46,560
有啊，呃，肯、肯·洪。
[观众笑声]
Yes, um, K-Ken Hom.
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

904
00:46:46,600 --> 00:46:48,640
观众1：肯·利文斯通。
- 肯·利文斯通。
MAN 1: Ken Livingstone.
- Ken Livingstone.

905
00:46:48,680 --> 00:46:50,440
呵，可真是帮了我大忙啊。
Oh, thanks for helping me out.

906
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:53,720
我的论点成立。现场还有人能想出
哪怕一个叫肯的酷人吗？
My case rests. Can anyone think
of a cool Ken?

907
00:46:53,760 --> 00:46:55,640
观众2：肯尼·鲍尔。
- 肯尼·鲍尔。
MAN 2: Kenny Ball.
- Kenny Ball.

908
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:57,040
越来越离谱了。
It's getting worse.

909
00:46:57,080 --> 00:46:58,800
这确实太难了。
- 我们这边有一个！
This is really difficult.
- We got one over here.

910
00:46:58,840 --> 00:46:59,960
呃，其实……
- 谁？
Well, actually...
- Who?

911
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:02,120
芭比和肯。
- 芭比和肯？
Barbie and Ken.
- Barbie and Ken?

912
00:47:02,160 --> 00:47:04,000
他连老二都没有！
He doesn't even have a penis!

913
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:06,880
哈蒙德：这倒是真的。
- 他底下就只有个鼓包。
HAMMOND: That's true.
- He has a mound.

914
00:47:06,900 --> 00:47:11,800
既然是叫肯的人设计的，那就只能“不酷”。
- 不过，我觉得这事儿有办法解决。
It's styled by Ken; that makes it Uncool.
- But, I think we could solve this.

915
00:47:11,820 --> 00:47:17,020
要是你恰好叫肯，而且觉得自己很酷，
那就写信给我们，地址是——
If, maybe you are a Ken, and you think
you're cool, so write to us at-

916
00:47:17,040 --> 00:47:19,340
[偷笑]
说不定真有呢，我是说……
[SNICKERING]
They might be. I'm a-

917
00:47:19,360 --> 00:47:20,560
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

918
00:47:20,580 --> 00:47:24,080
克拉克森：寄你们的照片过来……
- 把能证明你很酷的照片寄到……
CLARKSON: Send your photographs-
- Send us a photo of yourself being cool to

919
00:47:33,920 --> 00:47:35,840
那现在就剩下这一台了。
So that leaves us with this.

920
00:47:35,880 --> 00:47:39,120
观众：极酷！
- 阿斯顿·马丁 DB9。
AUDIENCE MEMBER: Sub-Zero.
- Aston Martin DB9.

921
00:47:39,160 --> 00:47:43,000
行，除了“极酷”，
还有别的说法吗？
Okay, can I hear anything
other than Sub Zero?

922
00:47:43,040 --> 00:47:45,680
还有比“极酷”更高的吗？
- 干冰！
Any advance on Sub Zero?
- Dry Ice.

923
00:47:45,720 --> 00:47:47,680
现场观众：零下40度！
- 零下40度！
AUDIENCE MEMBER: Minus 40.
- Minus 40.

924
00:47:47,720 --> 00:47:50,120
跟你们说，你们全猜错了。
Do you know, you're all wrong.

925
00:47:50,160 --> 00:47:51,480
哈蒙德：不酷？
HAMMOND: Uncool?

926
00:47:51,520 --> 00:47:55,960
它根本不在“极酷”区。
- 就是不酷。
It's not Sub Zero.
- Uncool.

927
00:47:56,000 --> 00:48:00,080
我们不得不单独为它造了一个新分区。
We have had to build a new section for it.

928
00:48:00,120 --> 00:48:03,760
DB9专属区——实际上就是台冰箱。
The DB9 section, and it's a fridge.

929
00:48:03,800 --> 00:48:05,360
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

930
00:48:05,400 --> 00:48:06,240
就在这儿。
There it is.

931
00:48:14,560 --> 00:48:16,080
完美。
Excellent.

932
00:48:16,120 --> 00:48:19,280
话说回来，莲花Elise的销量
Now, sales of the Lotus Elise

933
00:48:19,320 --> 00:48:20,920
近年来断崖式下滑，
have plummeted in recent years,

934
00:48:20,960 --> 00:48:23,360
于是莲花决定提振销量：
and Lotus decided to increase those sales.

935
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:26,640
“咱们破天荒头一回，
把它卖去美国吧。”
"Let's start selling it in America
for the first time."

936
00:48:26,680 --> 00:48:28,800
但为了做到这点，他们必须换一台新发动机，
But to do that, they had to put
a new engine in it

937
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:31,960
去应付美国那些蠢到家的
发动机排放烂规矩。
to meet all the daft American
engine emissions rubbish.

938
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:34,720
于是他们从丰田那儿掏了一台。
So they got one out of a Toyota.

939
00:48:34,760 --> 00:48:39,280
[观众笑声]
- 哎！别笑，这组合简直绝了。
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
- Ah! Don't mock, because it is an
amazing combination.

940
00:48:39,320 --> 00:48:43,080
丰田Celica的发动机
塞进这么小的一台车里。
Toyota Celica engine
in a little car like this.

941
00:48:43,120 --> 00:48:45,160
效果拔群，于是他们琢磨：“等等，
Worked brilliantly, so they thought,
"Hang on.

942
00:48:45,200 --> 00:48:49,520
既然这么给力，为什么不搞个硬顶、
That goes well, why don't we do a hardtop,

943
00:48:49,560 --> 00:48:51,000
硬核版本呢？”
hardcore version?"

944
00:48:51,620 --> 00:48:52,620
[直升机呼啸掠过]
[HELICOPTER BUZZES PAST]

945
00:48:56,640 --> 00:48:59,240
克拉克森：就是它了。
Exige。
CLARKSON: This is it.
The Exige.

946
00:49:00,920 --> 00:49:05,440
车重不足一吨，却能压榨出
190匹制动马力。
It weighs less than a tonne, but you get
190 brake horsepower.

947
00:49:07,400 --> 00:49:11,360
这就好比把土星五号火箭
塞进了家用搅拌机。
That's like putting a Saturn V
rocket in a food blender.

948
00:49:18,360 --> 00:49:22,000
零到六十英里加速只要4.9秒。
It does nought to 60 in 4.9 seconds.

949
00:49:24,120 --> 00:49:27,400
油门到底，能一路飙到147英里。
Flat-out, you'll be going 147.

950
00:49:31,560 --> 00:49:34,200
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

951
00:49:34,240 --> 00:49:36,600
而且这台发动机其实相当精密。
And it's actually quite
a sophisticated engine.

952
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:40,760
配备了两根凸轮轴，一根管省油，
一根管爆发力。
You get two camshafts, one for economy
and one for power.

953
00:49:40,800 --> 00:49:44,880
还有一套莲花的电脑，
负责在两轴之间进行切换。
And there's a Lotus computer,
which manages the transition
between the two.

954
00:49:46,600 --> 00:49:50,240
转速拉到6200转时，
You get to 6,200 RPM

955
00:49:50,280 --> 00:49:53,640
普通发动机这会儿早就泄气了。
when a normal engine would
be running out of steam.

956
00:49:53,680 --> 00:49:55,520
瞧好了。
Here we go.

957
00:49:55,560 --> 00:50:00,040
切到动力凸轮轴的那一瞬间，
能明显感到顿挫，猛地一蹿。
And there's actually a step, a jerk,
as it goes onto the power cam.

958
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:02,920
然后力道更加凶猛！
And you get even more!

959
00:50:05,240 --> 00:50:06,280
哇哦！
Whoa!

960
00:50:07,960 --> 00:50:11,400
而且最爽的是，当你降下一挡——
And the best thing is that
when you drop down a gear

961
00:50:11,440 --> 00:50:13,320
在这样的赛道上过弯，
to go round a corner on a track like this,

962
00:50:13,360 --> 00:50:15,160
只要你敢豁出去狠开，
when you're really going for it,

963
00:50:15,200 --> 00:50:19,600
转速就始终维持在
神奇的6200转以上。
it always stays above
that magical 6,200 rpm.

964
00:50:19,640 --> 00:50:22,960
所以动力永远随叫随到。
So you've ALWAYS got the power.

965
00:50:23,760 --> 00:50:26,560
[大笑]
[LAUGHING]

966
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:30,680
但奇怪的是，速度并不是
这辆车的精髓所在。
But strangely, speed is not the key
to this car.

967
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:36,600
而且尽管要价高达三万英镑，
它也谈不上半点高级感。
And despite the rather steep £30,000
price tag, nor is sophistication.

968
00:50:36,640 --> 00:50:41,800
当然了，当你手脚并用从里面爬出来的时候，
你看着也体面不到哪儿去。
Certainly, you don't look very
sophisticated when you're getting out of it

969
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:43,240
[偷笑]
[CHUCKLES]

970
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:47,040
再瞧瞧你刚爬出来的这套内饰。
And then, there's the interior
you've left behind.

971
00:50:47,080 --> 00:50:51,480
没错，它确实有个能放MP3的音响，有空调，
Yes, you've got a stereo that plays
your MP3s and air-conditioning

972
00:50:51,520 --> 00:50:53,600
还有电动车窗。
and electric windows.

973
00:50:53,640 --> 00:50:56,640
但这全都是加钱选配，地毯也是选配，
But all these things, are optional extras
and so are the carpets,

974
00:50:56,680 --> 00:50:59,520
甚至连遮阳板都得加钱选装。
and so even, the sun visors.

975
00:50:59,560 --> 00:51:03,120
想知道这玩意儿到底有多简陋，
To get an idea of just
how spartan this thing is,

976
00:51:03,160 --> 00:51:06,480
你只需往后车窗里看一眼。
you need to look through the rear window.

977
00:51:06,520 --> 00:51:11,080
后边就是铁丝网、锡箔纸，
还有特百惠塑料盒。
Back there, you've got chicken wire,
BacoFoil and Tupperware.

978
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:16,080
感觉就像是在偷看你奶奶家
那个老旧的厨房橱柜一样。
It's kind of like peering into one of your
granny's old kitchen cabinets.

979
00:51:16,120 --> 00:51:20,960
所以如果它既不图速度也不讲舒适，
那造这车到底是图个啥？
So if it's not built for speed or comfort,
what's this car for then?

980
00:51:20,980 --> 00:51:23,980
♪ Black Sabbath - Paranoid ♪
♪ Black Sabbath - Paranoid ♪

981
00:51:24,520 --> 00:51:27,160
呃……就是为了这个。
Well, um, this.

982
00:51:28,160 --> 00:51:29,320
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

983
00:51:30,960 --> 00:51:33,160
这车过弯灵敏得像只苍蝇！
It corners like a housefly.

984
00:51:33,200 --> 00:51:35,200
它不仅比Elise更强，
It's not just better than an Elise,

985
00:51:35,240 --> 00:51:37,520
它简直能把市面上几乎所有车都秒了。
it's better than just about anything.

986
00:51:37,560 --> 00:51:39,000
原因就在这里。
And here's why.

987
00:51:44,600 --> 00:51:46,840
前分流器和后扰流板
The front splitter and the rear spoiler

988
00:51:46,880 --> 00:51:51,120
协同工作，产生实打实的下压力，
就像F1赛车一样。
work together to create real downforce,
like you get with a Formula 1 car.

989
00:51:54,160 --> 00:51:56,280
它的轮胎是交规允许范围内最接近光头胎的，
Its tyres are as slick as the law allows,

990
00:51:56,320 --> 00:51:59,000
而且还配备了赛道级悬挂。
and you get racing suspension.

991
00:52:00,720 --> 00:52:04,920
把这些全部加在一起，
效果简直令人惊掉下巴！
Add that lot together
and the effect is astonishing!

992
00:52:06,240 --> 00:52:08,400
开起来简直丧心病狂！
Everything just goes mental!

993
00:52:08,440 --> 00:52:13,640
要找个能跟它匹敌的对手，
你得把思维往垂直方向发散了。
To come up with something to match it,
you have to think vertically.

994
00:52:13,680 --> 00:52:16,680
♪ John Murphy - Jim's Parents ♪
♪ John Murphy - Jim's Parents ♪

995
00:52:24,720 --> 00:52:26,240
这家伙兴许能行。
This might do the trick.

996
00:52:26,280 --> 00:52:28,600
一架阿帕奇武装直升机。
It's an Apache helicopter gunship.

997
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:33,240
它算不上世界上最快的直升机，
It's not the fastest
helicopter in the world,

998
00:52:33,280 --> 00:52:35,400
最高时速也就163英里，
it'll only do 163 miles an hour,

999
00:52:35,440 --> 00:52:38,840
机动性也绝不是最灵活的。
and nor is it the most manoeuvrable.

1000
00:52:38,880 --> 00:52:44,640
但它长得最丑，
而且杀伤力最为致命。
But it is the ugliest, and it does pack
the deadliest punch.

1001
00:52:44,680 --> 00:52:49,520
它配备了12枚地狱火导弹，
72枚火箭弹，
It carries 12 Hellfire missiles,
72 rockets,

1002
00:52:49,560 --> 00:52:52,520
还有一门机炮，飞行员眼睛看哪儿
炮口就指哪儿，
and it has a cannon which points wherever
the pilot is looking

1003
00:52:52,560 --> 00:52:56,960
射速高达每秒10发
高爆弹。
and fires 10 high-explosive
rounds a second.

1004
00:52:58,880 --> 00:53:03,600
不过阿帕奇最让我着迷的，
还是它的雷达系统，
The thing that interests me most of all
about the Apache though is its radar,

1005
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:07,480
因为你看，它能从八公里外的树林
或小山丘后面冷不丁冒出来，
because, you see, it can pop up from behind
a tree or a hill eight kilometres away,

1006
00:53:07,520 --> 00:53:09,560
扫视一眼战场，
it'll have a look at the battlefield,

1007
00:53:09,600 --> 00:53:12,800
瞬间识别出256个目标，
it'll recognise 256 targets,

1008
00:53:12,840 --> 00:53:16,840
挑出眼下威胁最大的
16个高危目标，
prioritise the 16 most dangerous
at that given moment

1009
00:53:16,880 --> 00:53:18,200
然后把它们统统炸上天。
and destroy all of them.

1010
00:53:18,240 --> 00:53:22,880
干完这所有的一切，只要28秒。
And it'll do all that in 28 seconds.

1011
00:53:22,920 --> 00:53:28,240
厉害吧。但在咱们的赛道上跑一圈，
它真能用导弹锁定咱们的路特斯吗？
Great. But in a single lap of our track,
can it get missile lock on our Lotus?

1012
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:32,280
全世界最强悍的武装直升机，
The best helicopter gunship in the world,

1013
00:53:32,320 --> 00:53:35,480
配上全世界最优秀的飞行员——
英国陆军航空兵。
flown by the best pilots in the world,
the British Army.

1014
00:53:35,520 --> 00:53:38,160
♪ 摩托头乐队 - 黑桃A ♪
♪ Motörhead - Ace of Spades ♪

1015
00:53:38,200 --> 00:53:40,920
对决全世界操控最好的跑车，
Against the best-handling car in the world,

1016
00:53:40,960 --> 00:53:42,320
驾驶者——一个大傻子。
driven by an idiot.

1017
00:53:44,280 --> 00:53:48,160
要是他们飞远点儿打，赢起来轻而易举，
但我们给飞行员立了规矩：
They'd win easily if they went a long way
away, but we've instructed the pilots

1018
00:53:48,200 --> 00:53:51,040
活动范围不得超出赛道空域。
to stay within the confines of the track.

1019
00:53:51,920 --> 00:53:53,040
克拉克森：出发！
CLARKSON: Let's go.

1020
00:53:55,760 --> 00:53:57,320
飞行员：目标已确认。
PILOT: Target is identified.

1021
00:53:59,040 --> 00:54:01,140
♪ 若你嗜赌如命 ♪
♪ 那就找对人了 ♪
♪ If you like to gamble, ♪
♪ I tell you I'm your man ♪

1022
00:54:01,160 --> 00:54:04,080
天哪，这阵仗可不是
天天都能见着的；
God, that is not something
you see every day;

1023
00:54:04,120 --> 00:54:07,960
后视镜里死死咬着一架武装直升机！
a gunship in your rear view mirror.

1024
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:11,080
我要掉头逆向开，
看看他们接不接得住这招。
I'm gonna turn around and go the other way,
hope they're ready for that.

1025
00:54:12,500 --> 00:54:15,780
♪ 玩的就是心跳 ♪
♪ 管你说三道四 ♪
♪ The pleasure is to play, ♪
♪ makes no difference what you say ♪

1026
00:54:15,800 --> 00:54:19,120
哥们儿，我这车可不是铁疙瘩坦克。
I'm not exactly a tank, matey boy.

1027
00:54:19,160 --> 00:54:23,760
因为它通体乌黑还是塑料车身，
雷达很难锁定它。
Because this is black and plastic,
it's hard to get radar lock.

1028
00:54:23,800 --> 00:54:27,280
简直就像一架F-117夜鹰隐形战机。
It's like an F-117 Nighthawk.

1029
00:54:30,080 --> 00:54:35,160
倒不是我像个没长大的熊孩子，
但这玩意儿实在太好玩了！
It's not that I'm an overgrown schoolboy
or anything, but this is really good fun.

1030
00:54:36,720 --> 00:54:40,400
我刹车比它晚，
过弯比直升机还要灵活。
I can out-brake and I can outturn
the helicopter.

1031
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:44,560
但只要我刚变向过完弯一秒半，
But one and a half seconds after
I've made the move,

1032
00:54:44,600 --> 00:54:48,040
一瞄后视镜，
砰！它又赫然冒出来了。
you look in the door mirror and,
boom, there it is.

1033
00:54:50,760 --> 00:54:52,080
[轮胎尖叫声]
♪ 要么加倍要么出局 ♪
[TYRES SCREECHING]
♪ Double up or quit ♪

1034
00:54:52,100 --> 00:54:55,300
♪ 押上双倍抑或拆牌分注 ♪
♪ 黑桃A ♪
♪ Double stake or split, ♪
♪ The Ace of Spades ♪

1035
00:54:55,320 --> 00:54:57,320
♪ 黑桃A ♪
♪ The Ace of Spades ♪

1036
00:55:01,000 --> 00:55:05,000
刚才我还一度钻到了它柔软的
美式机腹底下躲着。
At one point, I hid beneath its soft
American underbelly.

1037
00:55:05,020 --> 00:55:06,580
♪ 你知我生来认栽 ♪
♪ 嗜赌终归是蠢材 ♪
♪ You know I'm born to lose, ♪
♪ And gambling's for fools ♪

1038
00:55:06,600 --> 00:55:08,960
结果直接被螺旋桨的气流掀翻吹飞了。
But it just blew me out again.

1039
00:55:09,000 --> 00:55:11,080
下洗气流吹得我车都飘了！
The car is moving in the downdraught!

1040
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:18,000
♪ 可别忘了还有大小王 ♪
♪ And don't forget the Joker ♪

1041
00:55:20,280 --> 00:55:25,520
那架直升机是我这辈子见过
最丑的机器了。
That helicopter is the ugliest
machine I have ever seen.

1042
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:31,280
丑到极致，反而有种诡异的美感。
It's so ugly, it's almost beautiful.

1043
00:55:31,320 --> 00:55:33,880
出现在后视镜里的时候可一点都不美。
Not when it's in the rear-view mirror.

1044
00:55:41,880 --> 00:55:44,000
它就在我屁股后面！
It's right behind me!

1045
00:55:46,520 --> 00:55:50,240
哇哦！所以，那武装直升机
最后用导弹锁定你了吗？
Wow! So, did the chopper
get missile lock on you?

1046
00:55:50,280 --> 00:55:53,080
没有，他们根本锁不住。
这就是这台车神仙级的地方。
No. They didn't. That's how
amazing this car was.

1047
00:55:53,120 --> 00:55:55,000
飞行员后来跟我说，
I mean, I'm told by the pilot

1048
00:55:55,040 --> 00:55:57,040
要是真在实战中碰到那种情况，
他们直接就开……
that in that kind of situation, they would
have just used

1049
00:55:57,080 --> 00:55:59,080
呃，机炮把我和车轰成两截了。
the uh, cannon on me and cut me in half.

1050
00:55:59,120 --> 00:56:00,560
哟，真体贴，真棒。
- 拿机炮轰。
Ooh, nice. Nice.
- With the cannon.

1051
00:56:00,600 --> 00:56:03,560
但要说导弹锁定？这小玩意儿
居然真能躲掉。
But missile lock? This thing
can actually evade it.

1052
00:56:03,600 --> 00:56:05,960
简直绝了。
- 确实神了。
It's phenomenal.
- That is incredible.

1053
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:10,800
不过，有谁想看看，如果让直升机
按正规打法来会怎样？
But, who'd like to see what
happened when the helicopter
did what it's supposed to do,

1054
00:56:10,840 --> 00:56:13,840
就是从两英里外的树林后面
猛地钻出来，
and pop up from behind
some trees two miles away

1055
00:56:13,880 --> 00:56:15,960
在超远距离直接给他来上一发？
and have a go at him from there?

1056
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:17,600
【观众】：想！
AUDIENCE: Yes.

1057
00:56:19,880 --> 00:56:21,400
【飞行员】：目标进入视线。
PILOT: Target, my line of sight.

1058
00:56:21,440 --> 00:56:23,200
目标已确认。
Target identified.

1059
00:56:23,240 --> 00:56:25,960
正在追踪，雷达已锁定。
Tracking, radar locked.

1060
00:56:26,000 --> 00:56:28,920
导弹就绪。发射。
Missile armed. Firing.

1061
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:32,120
二，一，命中。
Two, one, impact.

1062
00:56:32,160 --> 00:56:33,680
目标已摧毁。
Target destroyed.

1063
00:56:33,720 --> 00:56:35,740
【观众欢呼】
【哈蒙德】：啊哈！漂亮！
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]
HAMMOND: Awh! Wow!

1064
00:56:39,800 --> 00:56:43,240
那……那简直堪称完美。
That- that was almost perfect.

1065
00:56:43,280 --> 00:56:45,520
就一个问题：你怎么没被炸得粉身碎骨？
Just one thing. How come you're not
in little tiny bits?

1066
00:56:45,560 --> 00:56:47,000
你动动脑子嘛。
Think about it.

1067
00:56:47,040 --> 00:56:49,040
人家可是英国陆军。
事实上，他们今天也来了。
This is the British Army.
Here they are, in fact.

1068
00:56:49,080 --> 00:56:51,880
当时上天的机组兄弟……开直升机的大佬就在那儿。
The guys that were in flight...
There's the guy that flew the helicopter.

1069
00:56:51,920 --> 00:56:53,520
顺便说一句，干得漂亮，太牛了。
Oh well done by the way,
that was incredible.

1070
00:56:53,560 --> 00:56:56,200
【观众鼓掌】
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

1071
00:56:56,220 --> 00:56:59,520
最重要的一点你得搞清楚：他们是英军，不是美军，
The important thing you have to remember,
being British, and not American,

1072
00:56:59,540 --> 00:57:02,240
他们可不会朝自己的盟友开火！
- 噢，倒也是，没毛病。
they don't shoot their allies!
- Oh, you're right. Yes.

1073
00:57:02,740 --> 00:57:07,660
这台Elise（其实是Exige）在赛道上成功躲过了导弹锁定。
The Elise(!) has managed to evade
missile lock in the track.

1074
00:57:07,700 --> 00:57:09,580
但要是跟我们赛道上
But how will it get on against

1075
00:57:09,620 --> 00:57:12,340
测试过的其他所有狠角色相比，
它表现又如何呢？
all the other cars we have
round here on the track?

1076
00:57:12,380 --> 00:57:16,740
我想，是时候启动一级戒备斯提格了！
Time, I think, to move over to Defcon Stig.

1077
00:57:16,780 --> 00:57:19,700
【克拉克森】：他弹射出发了！起步疯狂打滑，
CLARKSON: Away he goes.
Lots of wheel spin there

1078
00:57:19,740 --> 00:57:22,500
毕竟路面还带着几分湿滑。
on what is a slightly damp track.

1079
00:57:22,540 --> 00:57:25,260
要说直线马力，可能确实是Exige的致命短板。
Now, straight line power could be the
Exige's Achilles Heel.

1080
00:57:25,300 --> 00:57:29,260
但一进弯道它绝对能全数奉还！瞧瞧这走线！
But it really will make up for it
through the bends. Look at that!

1081
00:57:29,300 --> 00:57:32,300
♪ REO Speedwagon - Keep On Loving You ♪
♪ REO Speedwagon - Keep On Loving You ♪

1082
00:57:33,340 --> 00:57:37,860
哎呀，天呐。斯提格买了张
类似抒情摇滚合辑的唱片，
Oh, dear. The Stig has bought
a sort-of power-ballad album,

1083
00:57:37,900 --> 00:57:41,100
看来这一整季
他都打算放给我们听了。
which he wants to play
for us over this series.

1084
00:57:41,140 --> 00:57:43,260
不过倒是一点没耽误他开车。
Hasn't affected his driving though.

1085
00:57:43,300 --> 00:57:45,420
噢，他开始猛推进了！
Oh, he's pushing it!

1086
00:57:45,460 --> 00:57:47,980
好，切入锤头弯。
Okay, down to Hammerhead.

1087
00:57:48,020 --> 00:57:49,980
看啊，这车就这么死死咬在走线上。
See, look how it just sits on the line.

1088
00:57:50,020 --> 00:57:53,340
全油门。瞧瞧那姿态。快看！
简直不可思议。
Flat-out. Look at that. Look at it!
It's unbelievable.

1089
00:57:53,360 --> 00:57:55,760
♪ And I'm gonna keep on lovin' you ♪
♪ And I'm gonna keep on lovin' you ♪

1090
00:57:55,940 --> 00:58:00,380
要进Follow Through弯了。
他会松油门吗？他会收油吗？
Coming to the Follow Through.
Is he gonna lift? Is he gonna lift?

1091
00:58:00,420 --> 00:58:06,460
居然全油门横扫过
Follow Through弯，太让人难以置信了。
Absolutely flat-out through the
Follow Through, which is unbelievable.

1092
00:58:06,500 --> 00:58:08,980
湿滑沥青路配上近乎光头胎的轮胎。
Nearly slick tyres on wet tarmac.

1093
00:58:09,020 --> 00:58:12,100
本来该险象环生的。目前看来相当漂亮。
Should be tricky. Looking good so far.

1094
00:58:12,140 --> 00:58:14,500
他能稳住吗？这是倒数第二个弯。
Can he keep it together? This is the
penultimate corner.

1095
00:58:14,540 --> 00:58:17,220
会冲上草地吗？没有，救回来了。
Is he going on the grass? No. Kept it off.

1096
00:58:17,260 --> 00:58:19,660
最后一个弯。
The final corner.

1097
00:58:19,700 --> 00:58:22,780
噢，走得极其干净利落，
冲线！
Ooh, it's so neat and tidy
and across the line.

1098
00:58:22,820 --> 00:58:26,500
大伙儿可别忘了，那只是一台
1.8升排量、丰田发动机的车，
You've gotta bear in min that was a
1.8-litre car, Toyota engine,

1099
00:58:26,540 --> 00:58:30,780
还是在湿地赛道上顶着几乎光头胎跑的。
virtually slick tyres on a wet track.

1100
00:58:30,820 --> 00:58:32,500
所以要是它能……
So it would be

1101
00:58:32,540 --> 00:58:36,420
跑得比本田NSX Type-R还快，
就够不可思议了。
unbelievable if it went sort of faster
than a Honda NSX Type-R.

1102
00:58:36,460 --> 00:58:38,940
你们懂的，1分31秒6，对吧？
- 没错。
You know, 1:31.6. Yeah?
- Yeah.

1103
00:58:38,980 --> 00:58:43,380
而要是它能快过911 Turbo，
那就简直离大谱了。
And it would be ridiculous if it went
faster than a 911 Turbo.

1104
00:58:43,420 --> 00:58:46,420
后者在湿地上的成绩是1分31秒整。
Did it in 1:31, on a wet track.

1105
00:58:46,460 --> 00:58:51,900
而它跑完一圈只要1分26秒9。
- 啥？！
It went round in one minute, 26.9 seconds.
- What!?

1106
00:58:51,940 --> 00:58:54,300
这也……
- 太神了！
That is...
- That's amazing!

1107
00:58:54,340 --> 00:58:55,740
[观众鼓掌]
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

1108
00:58:58,380 --> 00:59:03,300
这可是我们在本赛道测试过
第六快的车，
That's the sixth-fastest car
we've ever had here,

1109
00:59:03,340 --> 00:59:05,500
而且排量才1.8升。
- 简直令人目瞪口呆。
and it's a 1.8.
- That's astonishing.

1110
00:59:05,540 --> 00:59:08,220
今天这一期节目也同样令人惊叹。
- 噢，确实。
And this has been quite
an astonishing show.
- Oh, yes.

1111
00:59:08,260 --> 00:59:11,740
武装直升机、狂飙去法国南部；而下周，
Helicopter gunships, races to the south
of France, and next week,

1112
00:59:11,780 --> 00:59:15,060
内容还会更加炸裂，
因为这家伙想装黑人，
it gets even more amazing,
'cause he tries to be black,

1113
00:59:15,100 --> 00:59:17,260
这位想扮粉嫩，
he tries to be pink

1114
00:59:17,300 --> 00:59:21,540
而我则能开着全新的迈凯伦梅赛德斯SLR，
以极度作死的高速在弯道狂飙。
and I get to drive much too fast round
corners in the new McLaren Mercedes SLR.

1115
00:59:21,580 --> 00:59:22,740
下周见。晚安！
See you then. Good night.

1116
